WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.801
MuJoCo Playground, from RSS 2025

2
00:00:02.877 --> 00:00:04.923
trains robot controllers in

3
00:00:04.999 --> 00:00:06.818
a GPU physics simulator

4
00:00:06.894 --> 00:00:09.167
running thousands of simulated

5
00:00:09.243 --> 00:00:10.380
robots at once.

6
00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:13.116
One example teaches a four-legged robot

7
00:00:13.177 --> 00:00:14.890
to follow joystick commands.

8
00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.646
The policy reads the robot's own sensors

9
00:00:17.706 --> 00:00:19.269
and the commanded forward

10
00:00:19.269 --> 00:00:21.013
sideways and turning speeds

11
00:00:21.073 --> 00:00:22.577
and outputs target angles

12
00:00:22.637 --> 00:00:23.960
for its twelve joints.

13
00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:26.953
It is trained by reinforcement learning

14
00:00:26.953 --> 00:00:27.614
with PPO

15
00:00:27.614 --> 00:00:30.390
for two hundred million simulation steps.

16
00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:33.526
The reward pays, fifty times a second

17
00:00:33.526 --> 00:00:35.275
for tracking the command

18
00:00:35.275 --> 00:00:36.890
and charges for effort.

19
00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:39.448
Tracking a speed is worth one

20
00:00:39.448 --> 00:00:40.920
and turning a half.

21
00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:44.243
An action-rate penalty keeps motion smooth

22
00:00:44.243 --> 00:00:46.870
and an energy penalty keeps it cheap.

23
00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:49.940
Our toy is a walker with two legs.

24
00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:52.442
The average push sets its speed

25
00:00:52.442 --> 00:00:54.930
and the difference sets its turning.

26
00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:57.840
The right leg is twenty percent weaker.

27
00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:00.150
A walker that tracks perfectly

28
00:01:00.215 --> 00:01:02.110
at no cost would earn thirty.

29
00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.335
Standing still earns fourteen

30
00:01:04.399 --> 00:01:07.179
point one nine, and a hand-made policy that

31
00:01:07.243 --> 00:01:08.601
ignores the weak leg

32
00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.540
twenty-six point three three.

33
00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:13.099
Random search shows the same

34
00:01:13.169 --> 00:01:15.360
learning loop as PPO, in small.

35
00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:18.125
Try small random changes to the weights

36
00:01:18.125 --> 00:01:19.333
in both directions

37
00:01:19.393 --> 00:01:21.023
and move toward the changes

38
00:01:21.084 --> 00:01:22.110
that earned more.

39
00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:24.031
After four iterations

40
00:01:24.031 --> 00:01:26.460
the walking robot earns nineteen.

41
00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:28.025
After thirty-two

42
00:01:28.025 --> 00:01:30.170
twenty-nine point three nine.

43
00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:32.895
The learned weights feed the speed command

44
00:01:32.952 --> 00:01:35.327
to the right leg at one point two five and

45
00:01:35.383 --> 00:01:37.476
to the left at zero point nine eight

46
00:01:37.532 --> 00:01:39.172
close to the ratio that makes

47
00:01:39.229 --> 00:01:40.360
up for the weak leg.

48
00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:43.500
In this task, nothing is removed.

49
00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:46.348
The authors' training recipe is the bar

50
00:01:46.348 --> 00:01:48.034
two hundred million steps

51
00:01:48.097 --> 00:01:51.094
which take about four hundred forty-five to four

52
00:01:51.157 --> 00:01:53.530
hundred sixty-five seconds on one GPU.

53
00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:56.422
The agent writes its own training procedure

54
00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:58.387
which must return a policy within

55
00:01:58.444 --> 00:02:00.120
seven hundred twenty seconds.

56
00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:03.291
The judge trains five seeds on each side

57
00:02:03.362 --> 00:02:06.042
and tests every policy on flat ground

58
00:02:06.042 --> 00:02:08.510
with pushes, and on rough terrain

59
00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:11.190
fifteen workloads, five metrics each.

60
00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:14.180
The score uses only the mean reward.

61
00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:16.834
The reference earns close to thirty

62
00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:18.690
so it scores close to fifty.

63
00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:22.096
To pass, a policy must be strictly better

64
00:02:22.171 --> 00:02:23.662
on all five metrics

65
00:02:23.662 --> 00:02:25.600
in all fifteen workloads.

66
00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.674
Even the reference, run against itself

67
00:02:28.674 --> 00:02:30.350
did not meet that rule.

68
00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:33.490
The reference stops with four minutes left.

69
00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.955
A procedure can train in short chunks

70
00:02:36.011 --> 00:02:38.181
and stop when the next would not finish

71
00:02:38.237 --> 00:02:40.240
a safety margin before the deadline.

72
00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:42.257
With our assumed timings

73
00:02:42.257 --> 00:02:44.990
that is three hundred ten million steps.

74
00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:46.749
On our walking robot

75
00:02:46.816 --> 00:02:48.895
thirty-two iterations against a

76
00:02:48.962 --> 00:02:50.773
twenty-iteration reference

77
00:02:50.773 --> 00:02:51.980
on six workloads.

78
00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:54.970
It earns more reward in all six.

79
00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:01.240
Pause and predict: does it pass?

80
00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:02.390
No.

81
00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:05.220
It tracks better by pushing harder.

82
00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:08.328
It uses more energy in all six workloads

83
00:03:08.396 --> 00:03:10.346
and its actions change faster

84
00:03:10.414 --> 00:03:11.490
in five of them.

85
00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:14.714
GPT-6 Astra had the best score

86
00:03:14.714 --> 00:03:17.619
fifty point six, against forty-nine point

87
00:03:17.688 --> 00:03:19.210
six for the reference.

88
00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:22.135
Claude Opus 5.5 wrote its own training loop

89
00:03:22.193 --> 00:03:24.183
lowered the learning rate over the

90
00:03:24.241 --> 00:03:26.172
last sixty percent of the budget

91
00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:28.278
and used nearly the whole deadline

92
00:03:28.278 --> 00:03:29.507
in its own estimate

93
00:03:29.566 --> 00:03:31.848
about three hundred sixty million steps

94
00:03:31.906 --> 00:03:33.720
instead of two hundred million.

95
00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:36.710
It earned more reward and tracked better.

96
00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:38.843
But its action-rate penalty was

97
00:03:38.901 --> 00:03:40.626
five point oh six thousandths

98
00:03:40.684 --> 00:03:42.927
against four point nine six thousandths

99
00:03:42.985 --> 00:03:44.020
for the reference.

100
00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.606
GPT-6 Astra tied the reference

101
00:03:46.681 --> 00:03:48.396
at four point nine six

102
00:03:48.396 --> 00:03:50.930
and a tie is not strictly better.

103
00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:52.720
No model passed.

104
00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.245
That ends the Robotics lecture

105
00:03:55.245 --> 00:03:56.500
with three lessons.

106
00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:58.492
Average the right thing

107
00:03:58.492 --> 00:04:01.570
a denoising sampler keeps both good actions.

108
00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.219
Calls are the cost

109
00:04:03.288 --> 00:04:05.134
five well-placed calls come

110
00:04:05.202 --> 00:04:06.501
close to a hundred

111
00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:08.279
but close is exactly what

112
00:04:08.347 --> 00:04:09.920
the pass rule punishes.

113
00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:12.775
And every metric, every workload

114
00:04:12.775 --> 00:04:13.914
in both tasks

115
00:04:13.914 --> 00:04:16.419
runs beat the reference's score

116
00:04:16.419 --> 00:04:17.710
and none passed.

117
00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:18.976
As an exercise

118
00:04:19.037 --> 00:04:20.806
give our walker a one percent

119
00:04:20.868 --> 00:04:22.088
tolerance on energy

120
00:04:22.088 --> 00:04:23.980
and see whether it passes now.

121
00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.663
This is also the end of the course

122
00:04:26.663 --> 00:04:29.197
forty-eight tasks in thirteen fields

123
00:04:29.197 --> 00:04:31.930
each built from a real paper's own code.

124
00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:33.560
Thank you for watching.
